    {
      "title": "Queensland anti-corruption commission investigated just 20 of more than 6,000 complaints in a year",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/29/queensland-anti-corruption-commission-investigated-just-20-of-more-than-6000-complaints-in-a-year-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Statistics showed there is ‘almost no chance’ a complaint made against a government department like the police would be investigated independently, expert says</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Queensland’s anti-corruption commission has investigated just 20 of more than 6,000 complaints of suspected corruption in the past year, as the state government comes under renewed pressure to implement a years-late recommendation to <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/nov/16/queensland-watch-house-whistleblower-labelled-dog-in-facebook-group-for-police\">end the practice of police investigating police</a>.</p><p>The statistic was revealed in Queensland’s Crime and Corruption Commission’s annual report, tabled in state parliament on Friday afternoon.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/29/queensland-anti-corruption-commission-investigated-just-20-of-more-than-6000-complaints-in-a-year-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-28T15:00:37"
    },
    {
      "title": "Further interest rate hikes could ‘devastate’ property market without easing unaffordability",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/29/further-interest-rate-hikes-could-devastate-property-market-without-easing-unaffordability",
      "description": "<p>With RBA predicted to lift cash rate for fourth time this year on Tuesday, experts warn a fifth – or even sixth – rise would be ‘overkill’</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Two or even three more Reserve Bank interest rate hikes would be “devastating” for the property market but still leave housing more unaffordable than ever as higher borrowing costs trump lower prices, experts say.</p><p>The RBA’s monetary policy board is widely expected on Tuesday afternoon to announce <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/28/rba-expected-to-hike-cash-rate-to-46-its-highest-level-since-2011\">an increase in its cash rate</a> to 4.6%, from 4.35%, in a decision that will add another $100 to the monthly mortgage interest bill on a $700,000 loan.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/29/further-interest-rate-hikes-could-devastate-property-market-without-easing-unaffordability\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-28T15:00:36"
    },
    {
      "title": "Larissa Waters steps down as Greens leader due to ill health",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/28/larissa-waters-steps-down-as-greens-leader-due-to-ill-health-ntnwfb",
      "description": "<p>Ballot for new leader expected next week after Waters quits to manage pre-existing kidney disease that has ‘declined significantly’</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Greens leader <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2025/may/15/larissa-waters-elected-new-federal-greens-leader\">Larissa Waters</a> has announced she will step down due to ill health, with a party room meeting scheduled for next week to choose her successor.</p><p>Waters revealed on Monday night she has been managing a pre-existing kidney disease, but that her health had “declined significantly over the course of recent months”.</p><p><strong>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/28/larissa-waters-steps-down-as-greens-leader-due-to-ill-health-ntnwfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-28T11:41:51"
