    {
      "title": "Plan for controversial $1.2bn datacentre in Sydney scrapped due to ‘emerging’ regulations",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/28/plan-for-controversial-12bn-datacentre-in-sydney-scrapped-due-to-emerging-regulations",
      "description": "<p>Developer Goodman Group says changes in government rules are behind decision to pull plug on ‘Project Mars’ in Lane Cove</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Plans for a controversial $1.2bn datacentre in Lane Cove in Sydney’s north have been withdrawn, with the developer blaming “emerging” regulations from the state and federal governments for the decision to pull the plug.</p><p>The “Project Mars” plans were withdrawn from the NSW planning portal on Monday, with the developer, Goodman Group, posting on its site that the policy and regulatory environment for large-scale datacentres had “evolved significantly”.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/28/plan-for-controversial-12bn-datacentre-in-sydney-scrapped-due-to-emerging-regulations\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-28T09:53:10"
    },
    {
